hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18477","Ismail narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Shabi who said: Abu Jubayrah ibn al-Dahhak narrated to me, he said: Concerning us it was revealed among Banu Salimah: And do not insult one another by nicknames, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah and none of us but had two or three names, and when one of them was called by one of those names they said: O Messenger of Allah, he angers at this, so it was revealed: And do not insult one another by nicknames."
